# The Windows runs a release needs (release.md section 8, I76). tests/win/vm-run.sh check COMMIT reads
# this file as committed in COMMIT and passes only when every row has one passing record
# for COMMIT and its TEST payload.json. VM rows use runs made with COMMIT's scripts
# (tests/win/vm-run.sh run SNAPSHOT SUITE --record) and must have no failed record. One row a line:
#   SUITE  ARCH  SNAPSHOT     ARCH: arm64, x64 (native) or x64-prism (forced x64 on ARM64);
#                             SNAPSHOT: its name (the rest of the line) or its {id}
# rb-win-template is ARM64. Run the platform and startup matrix with --arch ARCH --record.
# The native x64 PC checklist stays in by-hand.md (VR2, recorded separately). smoke checks
# vm-run.sh itself.
# worker: release checks take pc-win.ok from RB-KIT's auto record on the real PC (M6). The
# snapshot below is used by VM diagnostics, where worker.suite's cache-hit step SKIPs.
bootstrap  arm64  clean Windows
uninstall  arm64  clean Windows
update     arm64  clean Windows
platform   arm64  clean Windows
platform   x64-prism  clean Windows
startup    arm64  clean Windows
startup    x64-prism  clean Windows
worker     arm64  rekordbox 7.2.19 installed
